<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Film actor; long and irregular shooting days; studies acting between films. Has missed two or three working days each cycle for the past year because of pain and worries that this is costing her work [S]</item><item>In a committed relationship; plans to marry this summer. Wants children, but not for at least a year [S]</item><item>Alcohol: one or two glasses of wine at weekends, never more than three at a time; no cannabis or other drugs [S]</item><item>Tobacco: does not smoke [S]</item><item>Pain medicines and sleep aids: ibuprofen 200 mg, two or three tablets at a time, during periods without enough relief; an urgent care clinic gave her six hydrocodone and acetaminophen tablets two months ago, all used; takes over-the-counter diphenhydramine on bad pain nights to sleep. The state prescription monitoring program shows that single opioid prescription and no sedative prescriptions [S]</item><item>Sexual and reproductive health: one male partner; no previous pregnancies; condoms until now [S]</item><item>Supports: her partner, a close friend from acting class, and her drama coach; reading and acting class steady her. She decides who is told about her health [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

