    <code code="29545-1" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Physical findings Narrative"/>
    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1956-06-15; see the Vital Signs section. Mental status: Alert, warm and cooperative; speech normal; thought process organized; no psychotic features; no history of manic or hypomanic episodes; Mood low, worse in the days around her period; tearful when describing missed work; PHQ-9 score 12 with item 9 scored 0; GAD-7 8; no thoughts of suicide or self-harm, now or in the past. The physical examination is limited to the findings relevant to this synthetic episode. [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Structured safety assessment: current ideation absent, intent absent, plan absent, access to means reviewed: yes. Outpatient care. She has no thoughts of suicide or self-harm now and has never had them. Because pain, poor sleep and a moderate depressive episode raise risk, a brief written safety plan was made with her, with warning signs (feeling hopeless, not sleeping for nights at a time, wanting to use medicines to blot out the day) and what to do about each. Lethal-means counseling: no firearm at home; leftover medicines are to be returned to a pharmacy take-back site, and no opioid, benzodiazepine or sleep medicine will be prescribed. The 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline was given and saved in her phone, with the clinic number. Safety reviewed at every visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

